      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $6$ contain the integer $7?$\n\n- $[-5]_{6}$\n- $[3]_{6}$\n- $[1]_{6}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $7\\in [a]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\n7≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $7\\in [-5]_{6}$ because $7≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $7\\notin [3]_{6}$ because $7≢3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in [1]_{6}$ because $7≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
